{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"AITER’s exact primitive is correct but slower here because its API also writes the summed residual, adding an unnecessary full-tensor store. I’m staying with Triton and combining the two useful ideas: multiple independent rows per block (one reduction per wave) plus a persistent grid, which should reduce both cross-wave synchronization and block scheduling."}}
